  "body": "Found by the high-tier review of PR #1099 (2026-11-12, head `434a464a`, review comment on that PR). It is main's existing behaviour, not that PR's change, so it is filed on its own.\n\n**What happens.** The verify step's existing hole-wall allowance (the one that excuses a round tool on a faceted hole wall) decides by a facet's corners. A flat facet whose corners lie on the hole's circle passes well inside that circle along its middle, and material there can be cut without a blocking warning.\n\n**Reading (reviewer's throwaway probe, not in the tree).** Model hole: an octagon with its corners on r 5 mm. A Thread op declared at r 4.4 mm - outside PR #1099's new grant, so only main's allowance is in play - verifies with 0 blocking warnings while the cut goes 0.32 mm into each flat. The same octagon declared at r 5.3 gives 56 gouges, so the check does read that mesh. A Bore op probably has the same gap; that was not measured.\n\n**Why it matters.** A gouge that passes verify is the Prime Directive's worst case. A real part can carry such a hole: a D-bore, a hex or octagonal pocket, or a round hole imported so coarse that its flats are real within tolerance.\n\n**Where to look.** `crates/sim/src/verify/` (the hole-wall / bore-facet allowance; `bore_facet_sagitta` and `bore_entry` in `crates/app/tests/` pin today's behaviour). PR #1099 adds the same corner measurement in `thread_bore.rs` `wall_radius` and `material_source.rs` `major_rims`; its review asks for the nearest-point measurement there, and the two should end up with one rule.\n\n**Expected.** The allowance excuses only what a facet's sagitta explains: it is measured at the facet's nearest point to the hole's axis, and a facet (or outline edge) that passes inside the circle by more than the stated tolerance convicts.\n\nDone means: first reproduce the reading in a test (octagon on r 5, the op that shows it; also try a Bore op and a D-bore and say what each gives); then the allowance measures the nearest point, an octagon and a D-bore convict, a finely faceted round hole still verifies clean (the existing sagitta pins stay green without being loosened), and nothing else in the verify goldens moves without a stated reason.\n",
